#STARS#USUAL#


A1. What is it that just can't stand around without working? ~ CIDER
A5. Name something the censors find everywhere. ~ FAULT
A9. What stop sign is often used in the parlor? ~ DONT
A10. What prompted Antony's visit to Egypt (Latin)? ~ AMO
A12. Name something that's often in the soup (plural). ~ PEAS
A14. What do reformers do to most of us? ~ IRK
A15. Name something people never ride in more than once (plural). ~ BIERS
A17. What is the Venus de Milo? ~ ART
A18. What is a shorter printer's measure? ~ EN
A19. Name something that is always down in the mouth (plural). ~ PALATES
A21. What is an abbreviation for a word meaning "every one of any number separately considered"? ~ EA
A22. What was Peck's Bad Boy to his mother? ~ SON
A23. What should every flat tire get? ~ AIR
A25. What is found in all family trees? ~ SAPS
A27. What is a second-hand coal? ~ ASH
A29. What did Lindbergh do to keep up? ~ SOAR
A31. What are flappers' favorite fruits? ~ DATES
A32. What is it to praise greatly? ~ EXTOL
A33. Name something very little but very dangerous. ~ GERM
A34. What verb characterizes foxes and pawnbrokers? ~ SLY
A36. What does "throw out" mean? ~ EMIT
A38. Name a scandal catcher. ~ EAR
A40. What are "stuttering exclamations" (as written)? ~ ERS
A41. Who is the patron saint of the Wets? ~ AL
A43. Name a people who were born to blush unseen. ~ NEGROES
A46. What is the briefest abbreviation for "Hardy Wenches"? ~ HW
A47. Name something very moving. ~ VAN
A49. Who is noted for his hellish ways? ~ DEVIL
A50. From where do many people drive off? ~ TEE
A51. Name something sheepish (plural). ~ EWES
A53. Give a good name for a Scotchman. ~ MAC
A54. Who was the girl "nobody never done right by" in the good old mellers of yesteryear? ~ NELL
A55. What are skylights? ~ STARS
A56. What does customary mean? ~ USUAL

D1. What is much more pleasant to have on the hip than on the foot? ~ CORN
D2. What is it that, although black itself, is used to enlighten? ~ INK
D3. What is it that sometimes comes after the stew (init.)? ~ DT
D4. What is often on the fence? ~ RAIL
D5. What is useless unless it's fortified? ~ FORT
D6. Where do successful aviators stay? ~ UP
D7. What is always green in the spring? ~ LEA
D8. Name a well-known weed. (Not the one on page 12.) ~ TARE
D9. Name a way of making a good take-off (plural). ~ DIETS
D11. Name something procurable at certain filling stations. ~ MEALS
D13. Give the surname of a famous star. ~ STARR
D15. What is a proclamation of marriage? ~ BAN
D16. Name something that never dries up. ~ SEA
D19. What man is guided by the direction of strangers? ~ POSTMAN
D20. What girls does a man rarely ever take out? ~ SISTERS
D22. What is a good thing to have if you don't want to walk home? ~ SPARE
D24. What will you be sure to find in all the best houses? ~ ROOMS
D26. Name an American humorist. ~ ADE
D27. Name something that has a kick in it. ~ ASS
D28. What is the call of the Charleston? ~ HEY
D30. Who was the adopted son of Mohammed? ~ ALI
D33. Name one thing you can't make by starting at the bottom and working up. ~ GRAVE
D35. What is an insect in the first stage of its metamorphosis after leaving the egg? ~ LARVA
D37. What is good for a person who is all wet? ~ TOWEL
D39. What peril is Europe worried about? ~ RED
D40. What lives in water and most cross-word puzzles? ~ EEL
D42. Name something manufactured in large quantities by unskilled workmen in a large building in Washington, D. C. ~ LAWS
D44. Name something that should be without flaw (plural). ~ GEMS
D45. What four letters, if pronounced aloud, would frighten a thief? ~ OICU
D46. Greeley told young men to go West a few years ago. Where do they seem to be going instead? ~ HELL
D48. What used to be over the head of most girls—but rarely ever now? ~ NET
D50. Name a pre-Volstead beverage. ~ TEA
D52. In which continent is Montevideo (init.)? ~ SA
D54. What is the thirteenth letter in the Greek alphabet? ~ NU


